WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.085
Session identifiers and bearer tokens must
be protected because whoever can use them

2
00:00:09.165 --> 00:00:12.503
may be treated as authenticated.

3
00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:19.975
For cookie-based authentication,
attributes such as HttpOnly, Secure,

4
00:00:20.055 --> 00:00:27.209
SameSite, domain, path, and expiration are
part of the security model.

5
00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:34.085
HttpOnly helps keep cookies out of normal
client-side JavaScript.

6
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:38.934
Secure limits transmission to HTTPS
contexts.

7
00:00:39.014 --> 00:00:44.618
SameSite can reduce some cross-site
request behavior.

8
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:51.852
Domain and path settings influence where
the browser sends the cookie.

9
00:00:51.932 --> 00:01:00.993
Cookie-based authentication requires CSRF
risk analysis for state-changing requests.

10
00:01:01.073 --> 00:01:05.604
Browsers can attach cookies automatically,

11
00:01:05.684 --> 00:01:13.076
so an application should consider
anti-CSRF tokens, SameSite behavior,

12
00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:20.429
origin checks, and defense-in-depth
appropriate to the architecture.

13
00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:25.398
A same-site web app, a separate frontend
domain,

14
00:01:25.478 --> 00:01:32.512
and an API consumed by mobile clients may
each need different choices.

15
00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:40.461
The key is to understand how credentials
are sent and which requests can change

16
00:01:40.541 --> 00:01:41.257
state.

17
00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:49.325
CORS controls which browser origins may
call the application from client-side

18
00:01:49.405 --> 00:01:52.743
JavaScript under browser rules.

19
00:01:52.823 --> 00:01:57.950
It is not authentication, it is not
authorization,

20
00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.203
and it does not stop non-browser clients.

21
00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:09.556
Broad CORS settings are especially risky
when credentials are allowed.

22
00:02:09.636 --> 00:02:12.379
Cookie, CORS, CSRF, HTTPS,

23
00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:19.255
and proxy settings must match the actual
deployment architecture.

24
00:02:19.335 --> 00:02:27.800
Treat browser credential behavior and
cross-origin policy as one connected design

25
00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.980
rather than separate toggles.
